# ============================================================================
# Runtime state
# ============================================================================
# The app's own writable directory (config/paths.py data_dir()). Ignored in
# every app, which is the same statement as: nothing a fresh clone needs lives
# here. Anything a clone DOES need belongs in the repo.
# ANCHORED, and it has to be: bare `data/` matches at every depth, so it swallows
# frontend/src/lib/components/data/ and any other directory that happens to share
# the name — silently, since git never reports a file it was told to ignore.
/data/

# ============================================================================
# Household policy
# ============================================================================
# Raw dictation carries names that can't be scrubbed (core/pii-in-documents.md).
docs/development/voice-memos/

# ============================================================================
# App-owned
# ============================================================================
# Everything above this block is the factory's and is compared byte-for-byte;
# everything below it is this app's. Almost nothing belongs below: runtime state
# has one home (`/data/`, already ignored), and a rule about content the app
# tracks selectively is still this app's to write. What genuinely lands here is a
# file the app writes to the repo ROOT, which no other mechanism can reach —
# because git has no include directive, so this is the extension point.
# One reason per line, so a stale rule can be retired by someone who did not add it.
# App-owned below this line; the factory owns everything above it.
